# Day 10 – Generative AI Learning Journey
**Date:** 25 July 2026

## What I did today
- Designed an independent-play framework for my 6-year-old daughter
- Rejected the assumption that blocks are the strongest material
- Designed a 4-day Tiny Experiments protocol to test Blocks / Drawing / Dress-up / Puzzles under identical conditions
- Clarified how skills permanently store form templates across sessions
- Explored a self-QA loop so form-filling skills can reduce repeated correction cycles (capture → validator → auto-fix → permanent rule)

## What I learned
- Assumptions should be turned into experiments, not treated as facts
- Most form-filling cycles are caused by recurring errors that can be captured as permanent validators
- Skills remember templates permanently once packaged; only data needs to be supplied each run
- The same experimental discipline works for both banking systems and parenting systems

